        "patient": "A patient with established epilepsy screened positive for clinically significant depressive symptoms, with an NDDI-E score of 16. A neurologist and psychiatrist obtained a detailed anamnesis and applied ICD-10 diagnostic criteria in the assessment of depression. The depressive symptoms were not temporally linked to seizures and were not described as peri-ictal phenomena. There was no history suggesting that symptoms were attributable to antiseizure medication effects. On interview, no suicide risk was identified, and there was no suspicion of another psychiatric comorbidity. The clinical picture did not include psychotic features, and there was no evidence of bipolar disorder. The patient had not failed two adequately dosed and adherent antidepressant trials, and augmentation of antidepressant therapy was not considered necessary. The episode was not mild and was characterized as moderate-to-severe. The patient was pregnant, and after a documented risk–benefit discussion and shared decision-making, an antidepressant was not pursued. The primary clinical focus was management.",
